@{ViewData["Title"]="Disease intelligence";}<section class="intro"><div><small>PUBLIC HEALTH REFERENCE</small><h2>Understand water-related disease.</h2><p>Educational information for interpreting health surveillance signals.</p></div></section><div class="disease-grid"><article class="panel"><small>BACTERIAL · 01</small><h3>Cholera</h3><p>Can spread through water or food contaminated with Vibrio cholerae.</p><b>Signals to review</b><ul><li>Acute watery diarrhoea reports</li><li>Unsafe water exposure</li><li>Clusters requiring health-authority review</li></ul></article><article class="panel"><small>BACTERIAL · 02</small><h3>Typhoid fever</h3><p>Usually transmitted through food or water contaminated by infected faeces.</p><b>Signals to review</b><ul><li>Verified fever cases</li><li>Sanitation and water conditions</li><li>Official local health alerts</li></ul></article><article class="panel"><small>SYNDROMIC · 03</small><h3>Acute diarrhoeal disease</h3><p>A syndrome with multiple causes; community trends need clinical interpretation.</p><b>Signals to review</b><ul><li>Unusual report increases</li><li>Locality and age patterns</li><li>Healthcare facility observations</li></ul></article><article class="panel"><small>VIRAL · 04</small><h3>Hepatitis A</h3><p>Can spread through contaminated food or water and person-to-person contact.</p><b>Signals to review</b><ul><li>Clinically verified cases</li><li>Food and water safety reports</li><li>Public-health investigation updates</li></ul></article></div><div class="notice">These are educational references, not disease-specific predictions or diagnostic advice.</div>